-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Nov 21 21:32:18 UTC 2026 - Dirk Müller <dmueller@suse.com>

- update to 0.10.0:
  * Require Python 3.11 or later and support Python 3.15.
  * Require AnyIO 4.10 or later for `AsyncWebSocketSession`
  * Raise `TimeoutError` instead of `queue.Empty` when a
    synchronous receive times out (#139).
  * Return `bytes` consistently from synchronous and asynchronous
    `receive_bytes()`.
  * Enforce the configured limit on incoming WebSocket message
    size (Backported from httpx2#1085).
  * Unblock synchronous WebSocket shutdown when the receive queue
    is full (Backported from httpx2#1123).
  * Stop synchronous keepalive during WebSocket shutdown
    (Backported from httpx2#1228, regression test from
    httpx2#1229).
  * Ignore unsolicited and duplicate WebSocket pongs (Backported
    from httpx2#1122).
  * Translate ASGI WebSocket read errors during shutdown
    (Backported from httpx2#1233).

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Mar 29 12:17:49 UTC 2026 - Dirk Müller <dmueller@suse.com>

- update to 0.9.0:
  * Async exceptions are now wrapped in `ExceptionGroup`. Due to
    the switch to anyio.AsyncContextManagerMixin for cancellation
    safety, exceptions that propagate out of the async with block
    are now wrapped in an ExceptionGroup.
  * Fix #136: unclosed AnyIO queues after the ASGI transport was
    closed.
- update to 0.8.2:
  * ASGIWebSocketTransport: increase the initial receive timeout
    to 1 second and
  * make it configurable via `initial_receive_timeout` parameter.
    Fix #123

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Nov 13 15:14:59 UTC 2024 - Dirk Müller <dmueller@suse.com>

- update to 0.6.2:
  * Improve efficiency of WebSocketSession by reusing a single
    thread pool when waiting for messages
  * Fix (#73) anyio misusages
  * Fix (#74) unclosed anyio streams
  * Fix (#76) memory leak with non-async WebSocketSession

